WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:05.138
- [sighs]

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:06.673
- HEY, MAN,
THIS YOUR FIRST TIME?

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.007
- OH, MAN.

00:00:08.007 --> 00:00:10.844
I BEEN DOING ZOMBIE EXTRA WORK
ON THIS SHOW SINCE...

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:12.578
[chuckles]
DAY ONE, FIRST SEASON, MAN.

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:14.247
- MY FIRST TIME.

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:15.514
- OH, IT'S YOUR FIRST TIME
ON THIS SHOW?

00:00:15.514 --> 00:00:18.784
- MY FIRST TIME
BEING EXTRA AT ALL.

00:00:18.784 --> 00:00:20.320
- EVER?
- I'M KIND OF NERVOUS.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.921
- OH, WOW. OKAY, MAN.
HEY, MAN, IT'S...

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:23.790
THAT'S ALL RIGHT.
BUT YOU'LL BE ALL RIGHT, MAN.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.424
IT'S OKAY, MAN.
IT'S NOT THAT HARD, MAN.

00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:26.526
YOU'LL BE ALL RIGHT.
I'M--

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:28.094
ME PERSONALLY, DUDE,
I'M LOOKING

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:29.895
FOR THAT LUNGE BUMP, THOUGH.
[chuckles]

00:00:29.895 --> 00:00:32.064
- WHAT'S--
WHAT'S A LUNGE BUMP?

00:00:32.064 --> 00:00:33.633
- OH, THAT'S, UH,
LIKE IF YOU, UM,

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:35.902
YOU GET FEATURED
IF YOU LUNGE AT SOMEBODY,

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.703
AND THEN YOU GET
A BUMP IN YOUR PAY.

00:00:37.703 --> 00:00:38.971
AND IF YOU REALLY LUCKY, MAN,

00:00:38.971 --> 00:00:40.106
THEY BLOW YOUR HEAD OFF.

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:41.274
THAT'S STRAIGHT BANK
RIGHT THERE.

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:42.508
- ALL RIGHT, EXTRAS.

00:00:42.508 --> 00:00:44.810
I'M THE ASSISTANT DIRECTOR.
GATHER ROUND.

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:46.145
- JERRY, HEY, JERRY,
I HAD A THOUGHT, MAN,

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:47.346
ABOUT THE FIRST SCENE
THAT Y'ALL'S DOING--

00:00:47.346 --> 00:00:48.581
- NOT NOW, STAN.
- STEVE, IT'S STEVE.

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:49.749
- OKAY.
- OKAY.

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:51.550
- I NEED SOMEBODY TO LUNGE
AT THE FENCE.

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.420
- [growling]
- YOU THINK YOU CAN HANDLE IT?

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.355
- HIM?
- UH, YEAH.

00:00:56.355 --> 00:00:58.190
- IT'S HIS FIRST DAY, THOUGH.
HE KINDA NERVOUS, MAN.

00:00:58.190 --> 00:00:59.959
HE KINDA NERVOUS.
IT'S HIS FIRST DAY.

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:02.194
- OKAY, SO THE DIRECTOR'S
GONNA YELL "ACTION,"

00:01:02.194 --> 00:01:03.762
MACK'S GONNA COME BY,

00:01:03.762 --> 00:01:05.531
AND THEN YOU'RE JUST GONNA LUNGE
INTO THE FENCE, LIKE,

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:07.533
GRAAAH!

00:01:07.533 --> 00:01:09.502
- Y-YOU WANT ME TO SAY
"GRAAAH"?

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:10.603
- OH, THIS IS--
- SAY WHATEVER.

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:11.604
- THIS IS CRAZY.
OKAY, ALL RIGHT.

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:12.639
COOL, MAN--
HEY, YOU KNOW--HEY.

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:13.907
THAT'S COOL.
HEY.

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:15.074
HEY, YOU KNOW I GOT
A LOT MORE EXPERIENCE, MAN.

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:16.442
YOU CAN JUST USE ME.
I BEEN HERE...DAY ONE.

00:01:16.442 --> 00:01:18.244
FIRST SEASON,
SO IT--OKAY.

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:19.912
COOL, ALL RIGHT, THAT'S FINE.
YOU GONNA GO WITH HIM.

00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:21.247
ALL RIGHT, GOOD FOR YOU, MAN.
GOOD FOR YOU.

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:22.715
- GRAAAH? GRAAAH?
- NAH, DUDE, DO--

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:23.883
YOU DON'T HAVE
TO SAY "GRAAAH".

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:24.883
DO WHATEVER THE HELL
YOU WANT TO DO, MAN.

00:01:24.883 --> 00:01:25.885
- THAT'S THE LUNGE BUMP?

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:26.886
- THAT IS THE LUNGE BUMP, MAN.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:28.754
YOU GOT IT.
YOU GOT IT.

00:01:28.754 --> 00:01:30.023
ON YOUR FIRST DAY.

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:32.958
EVER BEING A EXTRA.

00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:33.959
EVER.

00:01:33.959 --> 00:01:35.428
YOU GOT IT, MAN.
GOOD FOR YOU.

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:37.230
- AND ACTION.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:40.232
[eerie music]

00:01:40.232 --> 00:01:43.235
♪ ♪

00:01:43.235 --> 00:01:44.237
- [high-pitched voice]
AAH!

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:46.405
WHAT'S UP, OBAMA, MY BABY?

00:01:46.405 --> 00:01:48.341
- WHAT THE HELL WAS THAT?
CUT.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:50.276
- OH, MAN, I WOULD BE
MORE THAN HAPPY

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:51.544
TO FILL IN, MAN.

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:53.145
I'D BE MORE THAN HAPPY
TO STEP IN.

00:01:53.145 --> 00:01:54.513
- MACK, JUST REMEMBER

00:01:54.513 --> 00:01:55.948
WHEN YOU'RE COMING
THROUGH THE FACTORY THAT,

00:01:55.948 --> 00:01:57.183
LIKE, YOUR MIND IS STILL
ON THE CAR OUTSIDE, ALL RIGHT?

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:58.283
- HEY, I MEAN,
Y'ALL GOTTA PICK PEOPLE

00:01:58.283 --> 00:01:59.418
BASED ON QUALIFICATIONS, MAN.

00:01:59.418 --> 00:02:00.453
- OKAY.
- HE DON'T HAVE ANY EXPERIENCE.

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.321
- IT WAS A GOOD NOTE,
GOOD NOTE.

00:02:02.321 --> 00:02:05.391
BUT MAYBE WHAT I WAS DOING
SORT OF SUPERSEDED THAT.

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:06.993
- AGREED.
YEAH, WE WERE JUST...

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.294
- YEP.
- DISCUSSING THAT.

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:09.896
ABSOLUTELY, IT SUPERSEDES IT,
YEAH.

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:11.697
BUT LET'S DO ONE
THAT JUST CEDES IT, OKAY?

00:02:11.697 --> 00:02:12.899
JUST SAME LEVEL.

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:14.167
WE'RE GOING AGAIN
STRAIGHT AWAY, OKAY?

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:15.768
- WOW, OKAY.
- RIGHT AWAY, RESET.

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:17.437
- HE'S NOT DOING
A GOOD JOB AT IT.

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:18.804
YOU'RE DOING GREAT,
THOUGH, MAN.

00:02:18.804 --> 00:02:20.306
OPPORTUNITY KNOCKS, YOU GOTTA
ANSWER THE DOOR, MAN.

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:21.974
- AND ACTION.
- WAIT TILL I TELL YOU.

00:02:21.974 --> 00:02:23.510
[growling]

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:26.512
[eerie music]

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:29.181
♪ ♪

00:02:29.181 --> 00:02:30.549
- [high-pitched voice]
ME-ME-ME-ME, ME-ME,

00:02:30.549 --> 00:02:31.718
ME-ME-ME-ME-ME-ME-ME!

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:32.785
- CUT.

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:35.121
- I'D BE MORE THAN HAPPY
TO STEP IN

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:36.522
AT ANY TIME
YOU WANT ME TO.

00:02:36.522 --> 00:02:37.756
I'D BE MORE THAN HAPPY
TO DO IT.

00:02:37.756 --> 00:02:39.558
- JUST A CERTAIN SENSE
OF URGENCY

00:02:39.558 --> 00:02:40.893
IS ALL WE'RE LOOKING FOR.

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:42.594
CLOCK'S TICKING, YOU GOT
SURVIVORS TO FIND, RIGHT?

00:02:42.594 --> 00:02:43.996
- CAN I TELL Y'ALL SOMETHING
FOR A SECOND?

00:02:43.996 --> 00:02:45.965
THIS DUDE RIGHT HERE IS NOT
DOING WHAT A ZOMBIE DOES.

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.933
THIS DUDE WAS LITERALLY
ON OUR LAST TAKE

00:02:47.933 --> 00:02:49.869
WAVING HIS HAND UP IN THE AIR
LIKE THIS, JERRY,

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:51.137
MAKING BEEKER SOUNDS.

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:53.840
HE SOUNDED LIKE BEEKER
FROM THE MUPPETS, Y'ALL.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.275
- THANK YOU, THAT'S GREAT.

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:56.643
JUST A TICKING CLOCK ON THIS
IS ALL WE'RE LOOKING FOR,

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:57.876
BECAUSE THERE ARE SURVIVORS,
IS WHAT WE'RE AFTER.

00:02:57.876 --> 00:02:58.878
- OKAY.
- OH, JEEZ.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:01.114
- BUT I FELT AMBIVALENCE
IN THERE.

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:03.683
- THE AMBIVALENCE IS ART.
IT'S GORGEOUS, AND WE LOVE IT.

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:06.218
BUT THERE ARE ZOMBIES, SO IF WE
COULD JUST PICK UP THE PACE,

00:03:06.218 --> 00:03:07.786
JUST A HAIR, THAT'D BE GREAT.
STRAIGHT AWAY, PLEASE.

00:03:07.786 --> 00:03:08.954
RIGHT AWAY.
- ALL RIGHT, GOING AGAIN.

00:03:08.954 --> 00:03:10.289
- JERRY, BUT JERRY,
WE'RE NOT DOING

00:03:10.289 --> 00:03:11.557
"NIGHT OF THE LIVING MUPPETS,"
ARE WE?

00:03:11.557 --> 00:03:12.658
- WE ARE NOT.
- 'CAUSE THE BEEKER

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:14.193
IS NOT A ZOMBIE.
- DO YOU HAVE ANY NOTES?

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:15.494
- YEAH, DON'T BE
A [bleep]ING BEEKER.

00:03:15.494 --> 00:03:17.363
- QUIET, PLEASE.
- ACTION.

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:20.199
[eerie music]

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:21.633
- [high-pitched voice]
I'M GONNA EAT YOUR BRAIN!

00:03:21.633 --> 00:03:22.635
ZOMBIE.

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:23.636
- CUT.

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:24.804
- NO!

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:27.373
HE ACTUALLY JUST SAID
THE WORD "ZOMBIE"!

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:28.874
COME ON, MAN!

00:03:28.874 --> 00:03:30.342
Y'ALL EVER HEAR OF A ZOMBIE
SAYING THE WORD "ZOMBIE" BEFORE?

00:03:30.342 --> 00:03:31.377
NO, YOU HAVEN'T.
I DON'T THINK SO.

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:32.912
- YOU KNOW WHAT?
GET RID OF THIS GUY.

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.880
- THANK YOU!
THAT'S WHAT I'M TALKING ABOUT.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:36.682
DUDE, I'M SORRY, DOG,
BUT YOU TERRIBLE AT THIS, MAN.

00:03:36.682 --> 00:03:38.050
- HIM.
- HEY, MAN, NO.

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:39.351
HE TALKING ABOUT HIM.
HE'S TALKING ABOUT HIM,

00:03:39.351 --> 00:03:40.419
'CAUSE HE SAID "ZOMBIE".

00:03:40.419 --> 00:03:41.420
- THANK YOU, STEVE.
- BECAUSE--NO.

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:42.588
NO, YOU WANT ME TO LEAVE?

00:03:42.588 --> 00:03:44.390
HEY, MAN, I BEEN UP HERE
STAGGERING AROUND HERE

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:45.525
FOR 3 1/2 YEARS,

00:03:45.525 --> 00:03:47.226
AND I BEEN STARTLING EXTRAS
LEFT AND RIGHT.

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:49.094
WHEN DO I GET
TO STARTLE THE LEAD, HUH?

00:03:49.094 --> 00:03:50.596
- ONE MORE FOR SAFETY.
STRAIGHT AWAY, HERE WE GO.

00:03:50.596 --> 00:03:53.766
- STILL ROLLING.
- ACTION.

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:56.836
[eerie music]

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:58.004
- HEY, WHAT DO WE DO

00:03:58.004 --> 00:04:00.373
IF WE HAVE TO GO
TO THE BATHROOM?

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:01.541
- WE LIKE IT?

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:03.309
- I LOVE IT. GENIUS. MOVING ON.
- I GOT IT.

